  "summary": "The first fab of JASM, TSMC's majority-owned joint venture with Sony Semiconductor Solutions, DENSO and Toyota, in Kikuyo, Kumamoto Prefecture. Announced in November 2021 as a 22/28nm specialty fab, it gained 12/16nm FinFET capacity and a higher planned output of 55,000 12-inch wafers a month in 2022, at an estimated cost of about US$8.6 billion. Japan approved a subsidy of up to 476 billion yen. Construction began in April 2022, an opening ceremony was held in February 2024 and volume production started in late 2024. In 2026 TSMC said it was adding capacity there for CMOS image sensor customers.",
